        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Guru Nanak</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1469 CE – 1539 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">15 April 1469, at Rāi Bhoi Dī Talvaṇḍī (now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nankana-sahib">Nankana Sahib</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>), a Bedi Khatri; another tradition gives the month of Kārtik (November)</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">22 September 1539, at Kartarpur, aged 70, after naming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guru-angad">Bhai Lehna</a> (Guru Angad) as his successor</span></div>
